Falsification for lane/hvf-spawn-destroy-gone (notes/job-mix/spawn-destroy-gone.md).

Restores `user_mode_runtime::yield_now` as it was before 2026-10-05: its own `asm!` block on each
architecture, declaring no output register. Expected with this applied:

  python3 helpers/syscall_asm.py      fails, naming the three yield_now blocks
  script/job-mix --hvf --release --smp 4
                                      refuses with -11 in a spawn job within a minute on
                                      patagonia (19 of 20 before the fix), because the spawn
                                      job's retry loop again loads DESTROY's arguments before
                                      the yield and traps with x0 = 0 after it

(The diff's context mentions milestone 299 (the x86 port-range capability), only because `outb`
follows `yield_now`.)

Apply with `git apply`, revert with `git apply -R`. Only yield_now is restored: it is the wrapper
the miscompiled loop crossed, so it is the one whose absence of a declaration this proves matters.

diff --git a/crates/user_mode_runtime/src/lib.rs b/crates/user_mode_runtime/src/lib.rs
